  "articleBody": "It's a common question for homeowners in Plano: when exactly should you call in a professional for a roof inspection? While many think about it only after a big storm or when they spot an obvious leak, a proactive approach can save you a lot of headaches and money in the long run. Texas weather is tough, and your roof takes a beating year after year from intense sun, hail, and strong winds. These elements can cause damage that isn't always visible from the ground but can compromise your roof's integrity over time.\n\nExperts actually recommend getting your roof inspected at least twice a year – typically in the spring and fall. These seasonal checks are perfect for catching issues that might have developed during the summer heat or winter cold. Beyond that, it's really important to get an inspection after any severe weather event, like a hailstorm, even if you don't see immediate damage. Hail damage isn't always obvious, and our team specializes in identifying those less visible signs. Also, if you're thinking of buying or selling a home, an inspection provides crucial information about its condition.\n\n**When Professional Guidance Helps**\n\n*   **After severe weather:** Even if you don't see damage, hail or high winds can cause unseen issues that shorten your roof's life. A pro can spot these. If you have insurance claim needs, we have expertise in restorations.\n*   **If your roof is older:** As roofs age, materials become more brittle and prone to cracking or warping. Regular checks help extend its life.\n*   **Before buying or selling:** An inspection gives you peace of mind or leverage during negotiations.\n*   **If you notice any interior water stains:** Don't wait for a drip; investigate immediately!\n*   **If you can't safely access your roof:** Steep pitches, brittle materials, or just safety concerns mean it's a job for the pros.\n\nDon't let small issues turn into major expenses. A timely inspection from a trusted local team like Discounted Roofing Co. can keep your Plano home protected.\n\n**What to Do Next**\nIf you're in Plano and wondering about your roof's condition, don't delay. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a professional inspection today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}